"""Public scientific contracts; contains no controller truth paths or values."""
DESCRIPTIONS = {
'denoise': '''Implement `tuso_model(adata) -> AnnData`. The input has count matrix in X and obsm['train'], with aligned cell and gene identifiers. Return the same cell and gene ordering and obsm['denoised'] of shape (n_cells,n_genes), finite nonnegative reconstructed molecular counts. Hidden evaluation independently normalizes each cell to 10,000 total counts followed by log1p, then computes MSE against independent hidden counts. Primary score clips 1 - method_MSE/no_denoising_MSE to [0,1]. An unchanged input is a valid zero-improvement baseline. Never return already logged values as molecular counts.''',
'label': '''Implement `tuso_model(train_adata, test_adata) -> AnnData or 1-D label array`. Training obs['label'] is public. Test labels are hidden. Return test_adata with obs['label_pred'] or a nonempty-string array of length n_test_cells, preserving test obs_names/order. Input gene alignment must be respected; use the public training set to fit the classifier. Expression is provided in X and/or layers['counts','normalized']. Primary score is the equal mean of accuracy, macro-F1, micro-F1, and weighted-F1 against controller-held test labels.''',
'batch': '''Implement `tuso_model(adata) -> AnnData`. Public obs contains batch and cell_type, as the upstream task permits biological covariates. Expression is provided in X and/or layers['counts','normalized']. Return unchanged cell identities/order and either layers['corrected_counts'] with input matrix shape, obsm['X_emb'] with shape (n_cells,n_components), or both neighbor matrices obsp['connectivities'] and obsp['distances']. All values must be finite. Corrected-count-only outputs undergo upstream PCA (50 components, ARPACK, no HVG filtering or further normalization); embeddings without a neighbor graph undergo Scanpy neighbors(use_rep='X_emb'). Primary score averages graph connectivity, rescaled biological-label ASW, and batch ASW within cell types. Graph-only output cannot support the selected ASW metrics without an embedding, because upstream has no graph-to-embedding transform. Provide an embedding or corrected counts for full scoring.''',
'svg': '''Implement `tuso_model(adata) -> AnnData` (in-place return None is also accepted). Inputs contain expression X/count layers and spatial coordinates, with gene identifiers. The true spatial variability annotation is hidden. Return var['pred_spatial_var_score'] in exactly the input gene order. The released TusoAI evaluator treats predictions as binary 0/1 labels and averages macro/micro AUC and macro/micro F1; continuous unthresholded values are not valid for this released classification contract. Literal binary accuracy is additionally reported separately. This released metric is not yet verified equivalent to the paper's Accuracy column. Optimize only the released score.''',
'decomp': '''Implement `tuso_model(single_cell_adata, spatial_adata) -> AnnData or array`. The reference single-cell input has public obs['cell_type'] and expression counts. Spatial expression has no true proportions; spatial_adata.uns['cell_type_names'] fixes output column order. Return spatial_adata.obsm['proportions_pred'] or array of shape (n_spots,n_cell_types), with finite nonnegative proportions that sum to 1 per row. Preserve spot identities/order and cell-type column order. Controller computes uniform-average R2 against hidden proportions and normalizes against a fixed reference-frequency Dirichlet control, clipped to [0,1]; raw R2 is retained. Fit only from visible expression and labeled reference cells.''',
'visual': '''Implement `tuso_model(adata) -> AnnData or 2-D array`. Input contains expression X and/or layers['normalized','counts']; cell-type labels, waypoints, reference distances, and evaluation metadata are hidden. Return obsm['X_emb'] of shape (n_cells,2), or an array with that shape, preserving cell identities/order and finite coordinates. Controller uses historical official OpenProblems metrics: trustworthiness(k=15), Spearman correlation of all pair distances after TruncatedSVD(500, random_state=0) on normalized input versus 2-D output, and UMAP density preservation(k=30, seed=42). The score averages trustworthiness and the two correlations rescaled to [0,1]. No labels, waypoints or centroids are needed. The metric requires at least 500 cells and 500 input features and uses every cell without subsampling. Raw three components are reported; equal weighting and correlation rescaling are declared reconstructions, not proof of equivalence to the published target. No labels or private reference distances may be used to fit the embedding.'''
}

def readme(task, names):
    return ('# OpenProblems: ' + task + '\n\n' + DESCRIPTIONS[task] + '\n\n'
            'Edit `solution.py` to implement the function. The starter `run.py` reads DATA_DIR and writes OUTPUT_DIR, executes the function on every listed dataset, and serializes the declared outputs. You may improve helper code, but preserve this complete external contract and regenerate predictions from source. The optimization dataset denominator is: ' + ', '.join(names) + '. Scores average datasets equally. Only these public inputs are available; no deployment scores or hidden targets are supplied. Algorithm search seed is 0. The complete frozen program will later run on separate deployment datasets without further adaptation to their scores.\n')
